# Internationalization (i18n) Conventions

## 1. next-intl (i18n)

- All user-facing strings MUST use next-intl. NEVER hardcode text.
- Translations live in messages/ (e.g., messages/en/common.json, messages/vi/common.json).
- Use useTranslations() in Client Components and getTranslations() in Server Components.
- Format dates/numbers with useFormatter() or getFormatter().

```tsx
// Server Component
import { getTranslations } from 'next-intl/server'

export default async function HomePage(): Promise<JSX.Element> {
  const t = await getTranslations('HomePage')
  return <h1>{t('title')}</h1>
}
```

```tsx
// Client Component
'use client'
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl'

export function Greeting(): JSX.Element {
  const t = useTranslations('Greeting')
  return <p>{t('hello')}</p>
}
```
